var VB_REFERENCE_HEAD='REFERENCE (EXAMPLE ONLY): the sample script below is about a DIFFERENT product. Follow its structure (what each part does, in the same order), sentence rhythm, tone and dialect words. Mirror its sentence length, but always stay inside LENGTH. Never reuse its product, scenario, jokes, benefits or exact phrases, and never mention its product. Product, use, daily problem and benefits come ONLY from DATA (benefits only from its advantages), and the script must say the product name from DATA. Pronouns and address follow Greeting/REGISTER, not the sample. If the sample tone or accent differs from DATA, use it for structure only. If a rule below conflicts with the sample, the rule wins. If a REVISION note includes a CURRENT SCRIPT, keep its wording and change only what the note asks.\n';
